  "notes": "Cube -> eight jittered corners -> wedge taper -> one-segment bevel (offset 8 mm) -> poke every face and lift its centre along the normal -> 1.5 mm sine displacement: 96 triangles, one closed shell, no boolean.  Taper narrows the point end to 60% in y and 46% in z and lifts it 4.5 mm.  Corner offsets are a fixed table (2-5 mm) so no two edges are parallel.  Materials follow the struck planes, not a height band: the top plane and the bevel facets that share its orientation (parent normal n.z > 0.35) keep the pale weathered cortex, the front/side struck planes are the fresh dark flint, and the point end (n.x > 0.85) plus the resting base (n.z < -0.85) are the dark iron-stained slot.  fit_bounds pins 70 x 55 x 45 mm.",
